{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"sapient-corrosive-puma","creation_channel":"cli","description":"The packaged code-review guide (`rebar explain review`, source\n`src/rebar/_guides/passing-code-review.md`) is the primary contributor/agent on-ramp for\nthe Gerrit LLM-Review gate — AGENTS.md points at it directly. Ticket bb9b landed the\ncontributor-triggerable re-review (comment `recheck-review` on a change; merged as Gerrit\nchange 1243, live in production), and docs/review-policy.md, CONTRIBUTING.md and the\nreview-bot runbook were updated with it — but the packaged guide was missed: lines\n112–114 still tell the contributor a coverage-gap BLOCK requires \"a maintainer\nre-triggers; re-pushing the same commit or pinging the maintainer is the move\". That is\nnow wrong (self-service exists) and it is the single most discoverable surface, so the\nstale text actively misdirects contributors to ping maintainers.\n\n## What\n\nUpdate `src/rebar/_guides/passing-code-review.md`'s coverage-gap bullet (§\"Reading the\nvote\", lines ~112–114) to say: a coverage-gap `-1` is an infrastructure veto, not your\ndiff — once the infra issue clears, comment **`recheck-review`** on the change to\nre-trigger the review yourself (the bot refuses only when the standing `-1` is a real\nfinding); mention that `recheck` (CI) and `recheck-review` (LLM review) mirror each\nother, consistent with CONTRIBUTING.md §2c and docs/review-policy.md. Keep the guide's\nexisting tone and line-wrap discipline. Doc-only change: no code, no tests to add;\nvalidation is `make lint` (format/whitespace) and grepping the rendered guide via\n`rebar explain review` in the worktree venv.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1: `src/rebar/_guides/passing-code-review.md` coverage-gap bullet names `recheck-review` as the contributor self-service re-trigger and no longer instructs pinging a maintainer as the primary move.\n- [ ] AC2: The change is merged via Gerrit with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1, carrying the rebar-ticket trailer.\n- [ ] AC3: `rebar explain review` run from the updated worktree shows the new text (packaged guide ships from source, no build step needed).","id":"f418-1b22-43f0-47ff","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Update packaged code-review guide for recheck-review"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785724528154420001,"uuid":"56bb0cb1-670d-4f10-856c-fe61f632ed1a"}